# Testing & evaluation

- Add/update tests for meaningful changes; focus on behavior and failure paths.
- Keep tests deterministic; no reliance on real external providers by default.
- Development checks: changed-file Ruff/lint/format, relevant type checks, affected pytest/
  Vitest modules and reachable API/browser checks for changed journeys. Expand only for a
  concrete adjacent risk or required gate; do not run complete suites after individual fixes.
- Batch related fixes and publication; reuse green evidence only for equivalent relevant
  revision/configuration/dependency/input scope. Preserve meaningful required PR checks.
- Full backend acceptance and combined validation follow `.ai/RELEASE.md`: freeze the
  reviewed candidate, satisfy coordinated staging and fresh SFP prerequisites, then perform
  the single explicitly requested `full_backend=true` gate. No full CI during repairs.
- Evaluation harness (deterministic/mock): `evaluate_agent.py`, `evaluate_rag.py`,
  `evaluate_guardrails.py`. Real-provider evals must be env-guarded and isolated.
- Do not lower coverage of safety, refusal, or approval-gating paths.
- Record exact tested SHA, executed counts, failures and skips. Component/mock, integrated,
  deployed and live-accepted results are different evidence levels; a merge is not deployment.
